Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","02.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":233,"path":234,"stem":235,"icon":236},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","02.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":238,"title":205,"body":239,"description":1211,"extension":1212,"links":1213,"meta":1214,"navigation":1215,"path":206,"seo":1216,"stem":207,"__hash__":1217},"docs\u002F02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format.md",{"type":240,"value":241,"toc":1194},"minimark",[242,246,250,254,265,272,276,286,292,296,301,304,343,347,354,361,367,371,378,433,439,449,462,526,529,597,600,604,607,613,617,620,626,630,633,639,643,650,890,894,900,1101,1105,1190],[243,244,25],"h2",{"id":245},"overview",[247,248,249],"p",{},"A CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier) is used by Kinotic to route requests to the appropriate service, method, or event stream. It is a URI-like format with parts named for clarity within the Kinotic platform.",[243,251,253],{"id":252},"format","Format",[255,256,261],"pre",{"className":257,"code":259,"language":260},[258],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@][zone~]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[262,263,259],"code",{"__ignoreMap":264},"",[247,266,267,268,271],{},"Everything in brackets (",[262,269,270],{},"[]",") is optional.",[243,273,275],{"id":274},"case","Case",[247,277,278,279,282,283,285],{},"Every part keeps the case it was written with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[262,280,281],{},"OrderService"," and ",[262,284,281],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[255,287,290],{"className":288,"code":289,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~org.kinotic.management.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[262,291,289],{"__ignoreMap":264},[243,293,295],{"id":294},"components","Components",[297,298,300],"h3",{"id":299},"scheme","Scheme",[247,302,303],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[305,306,307,319],"table",{},[308,309,310],"thead",{},[311,312,313,316],"tr",{},[314,315,300],"th",{},[314,317,318],{},"Description",[320,321,322,333],"tbody",{},[311,323,324,330],{},[325,326,327],"td",{},[262,328,329],{},"srv",[325,331,332],{},"Published services and their methods",[311,334,335,340],{},[325,336,337],{},[262,338,339],{},"stream",[325,341,342],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[297,344,346],{"id":345},"scope","Scope",[247,348,349,350,353],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[262,351,352],{},"@"," symbol.",[247,355,356,357,360],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[262,358,359],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[255,362,365],{"className":363,"code":364,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[262,366,364],{"__ignoreMap":264},[297,368,370],{"id":369},"zone","Zone",[247,372,373,374,377],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[262,375,376],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[305,379,380,388],{},[308,381,382],{},[311,383,384,386],{},[314,385,370],{},[314,387,318],{},[320,389,390,403,413,423],{},[311,391,392,397],{},[325,393,394],{},[262,395,396],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[325,398,399,400,360],{},"One application's services. Only that application's participants and the owning organization's runtimes can call them, through the app server, the one server that reaches these zones; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[262,401,402],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[311,404,405,410],{},[325,406,407],{},[262,408,409],{},"app-api",[325,411,412],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[311,414,415,420],{},[325,416,417],{},[262,418,419],{},"management-api",[325,421,422],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[311,424,425,430],{},[325,426,427],{},[262,428,429],{},"system-api",[325,431,432],{},"The system's own services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[247,434,435,436,438],{},"A cluster member outside the platform's servers can host its services in ",[262,437,419],{},", where organizations' users call them through the management server as they call the platform's own; such a service checks the caller's organization itself.",[247,440,441,442,445,446,448],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[262,443,444],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[262,447,429],{}," is rejected.",[247,450,451,452,454,455,458,459,461],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[262,453,402],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[262,456,457],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[262,460,376],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[305,463,464,477],{},[308,465,466],{},[311,467,468,471,474],{},[314,469,470],{},"Participant",[314,472,473],{},"May send to",[314,475,476],{},"May subscribe to",[320,478,479,495,514],{},[311,480,481,484,492],{},[325,482,483],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[325,485,486,488,489],{},[262,487,409],{},", ",[262,490,491],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[325,493,494],{},"reply destinations only",[311,496,497,500,509],{},[325,498,499],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[325,501,502,488,504,488,506],{},[262,503,419],{},[262,505,409],{},[262,507,508],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[325,510,511,513],{},[262,512,508],{}," — its applications' zones",[311,515,516,519,522],{},[325,517,518],{},"SYSTEM",[325,520,521],{},"everything",[325,523,524],{},[262,525,429],{},[247,527,528],{},"Each server also has a zone partitioning, the zones it hosts and the zones it reaches. A node advertises a service\nto the cluster only in a zone its server hosts, and sends only to zones its server reaches: an address in any\nother zone has no handlers there. An address without a zone passes both.",[305,530,531,544],{},[308,532,533],{},[311,534,535,538,541],{},[314,536,537],{},"Server",[314,539,540],{},"Hosts",[314,542,543],{},"Reaches",[320,545,546,563,580],{},[311,547,548,551,555],{},[325,549,550],{},"org",[325,552,553],{},[262,554,419],{},[325,556,557,488,559,488,561],{},[262,558,419],{},[262,560,429],{},[262,562,409],{},[311,564,565,568,574],{},[325,566,567],{},"system",[325,569,570,488,572],{},[262,571,429],{},[262,573,419],{},[325,575,576,488,578],{},[262,577,429],{},[262,579,419],{},[311,581,582,584,591],{},[325,583,444],{},[325,585,586,488,588],{},[262,587,409],{},[262,589,590],{},"app.*",[325,592,593,488,595],{},[262,594,409],{},[262,596,590],{},[247,598,599],{},"The gateway applies the partitioning before a frame reaches the event bus: a send to a zone the server does not\nreach, or a subscription in a zone it does not host, is refused whatever the participant may address. The\nservice directory and listener monitors still see every registration in the cluster, so a service hosted by one\nserver shows as online from any other, while each server's MCP listing shows only the tools in zones it reaches.",[297,601,603],{"id":602},"resource-name","Resource Name",[247,605,606],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[255,608,611],{"className":609,"code":610,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\n",[262,612,610],{"__ignoreMap":264},[297,614,616],{"id":615},"path","Path",[247,618,619],{},"An optional path that identifies a specific part of the resource, such as a method name on a service. The path's case is preserved.",[255,621,624],{"className":622,"code":623,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[262,625,623],{"__ignoreMap":264},[297,627,629],{"id":628},"version","Version",[247,631,632],{},"An optional semantic version for the resource. Enables versioned service routing so multiple versions of a service can coexist.",[255,634,637],{"className":635,"code":636,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById#1.0.0\nsrv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService#2.0.0\n",[262,638,636],{"__ignoreMap":264},[243,640,642],{"id":641},"factory-function","Factory Function",[247,644,645,646,649],{},"The ",[262,647,648],{},"createCRI"," function provides several overloads for constructing CRI instances:",[255,651,655],{"className":652,"code":653,"language":654,"meta":264,"style":264},"language-typescript shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","import { createCRI } from '@kinotic-ai\u002Fcore'\n\n\u002F\u002F From a raw string\nconst cri1 = createCRI('srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById#1.0.0')\n\n\u002F\u002F From scheme and resource name (which may carry a zone)\nconst cri2 = createCRI('srv', 'management-api~com.example.UserService')\n\n\u002F